From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: maxjivi05 <maxjividen@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Load 32-bit executables at their preferred base.

The pending "Dynamically relocate .exes by default too" patch moves every
.exe that has relocations and IMAGE_DLLCHARACTERISTICS_DYNAMIC_BASE to an
address the server picks from the top of the address space. For a 32-bit
program that is just below 2 GB: a test .exe with the usual 0x400000 base
loads at 0x7bfb0000 on DroidDeck-Proton, while Valve's Proton, upstream
Wine and the same prefix's free 0x400000 all leave it at 0x400000.

Older 32-bit games and their loaders expect their executables at the
image base. DiRT 2's launcher stops at once with its own report of a
breakpoint at 0x0041452A; it runs on Proton Experimental, which loads
the game at 0x400000. The patch's companion already notes that some
32-bit programs break when their executable is moved that high, but it
leaves them relocated unless WINE_DISABLE_EXE_ASLR=1 is set per game.

Keep executable relocation, and its WINE_DISABLE_EXE_ASLR switch, for
64-bit images, which the modding and hooking tools it was added for use.
Map 32-bit executables at their preferred base as Wine does upstream;
DLLs are unchanged.
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -3670,8 +3670,8 @@
     }
 
     if (!image_info->map_addr &&
-        ((image_info->image_charact & IMAGE_FILE_DLL) || !disable_exe_aslr ||
-         strcmp( disable_exe_aslr, "1" )) &&
+        ((image_info->image_charact & IMAGE_FILE_DLL) ||
+         (is_machine_64bit( image_info->machine ) && (!disable_exe_aslr || strcmp( disable_exe_aslr, "1" )))) &&
         (image_info->image_flags & IMAGE_FLAGS_ImageDynamicallyRelocated))
     {
         SERVER_START_REQ( get_image_map_address )
-- 
